## Environment variables

| Variable | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `TYPE_MCP_BASE_URL` | Upstream API base URL |
| `TYPE_MCP_ALLOW_PROTECTED_OPERATIONS` | Comma-separated exact operation IDs allowed for protected-write tools |
| `TYPE_MCP_API_KEY` | Optional bearer token (read at runtime, never logged) |

## Safety

- Protected-write operations require explicit allowlisting via
  `TYPE_MCP_ALLOW_PROTECTED_OPERATIONS`.  Wildcards, duplicates, unknown IDs,
  and empty values fail closed **before** any request is constructed.
- Denied operations exist as tools but always return a safe error.
- Generated tools never expose stacks, credentials, or raw upstream bodies.
